# ESLint cache. `npm run lint` is a bare `eslint`, and ESLint deletes a stale
# cache file when caching is off, so a tracked one reappears as a deletion for
# everyone who runs the gate. It also trips `design-lint --since`, which
# refuses on a dirty tree. Untracked here; see the PR for the measurement.
.eslintcache

# Local verification probes. Scratch, never part of a change.
.verify/
.verify-*.mjs
# The scratchpad directory agents are told to namespace their work under.
#
# It was NOT ignored, and on 2026-08-28 five worktrees held Playwright
# storage-state files containing live session cookies for the test account,
# alongside 243 PNG captures of signed-in surfaces. One `git add -A` in any
# of those trees would have staged a session token into a public repository.
# Nothing was committed; the exposure was potential and is now closed.
#
# Also a gate conflict, which is how it surfaced: eslint's default ignores
# cover node_modules and .git only, so scratch scripts here landed in the
# lint path and failed a gate on a change that touched only images and
# Markdown.
#
# Root-anchored like its neighbours above, for the reason stated there.
/scratchpad/
